{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y` (the rat weights, represented in `data_safe.json` as a row-major vector of length `N * T`).

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reshaped the original `matrix[N, T] y` to `vector[N * T] y` so the likelihood can be written as one plain vectorized sampling statement, `y ~ normal(mu_y, sigma_y)`, rather than nested sampling statements. The deterministic relation is `y[(n - 1) * T + t] = original_y[n, t]` for `n = 1..N` and `t = 1..T`. Moved the deterministic construction of `alpha`, `beta`, and the likelihood mean into the model block after the existing priors. No priors or likelihood terms were changed.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  int<lower=1> T;
  vector[T] time;
  vector[N * T] y;
}
parameters {
  real mu_alpha;
  real mu_beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma_beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
  vector[N] alpha_raw;
  vector[N] beta_raw;
}
model {
  vector[N] alpha;
  vector[N] beta;
  vector[N * T] mu_y;

  mu_alpha ~ normal(50, 20);
  mu_beta ~ normal(7, 5);
  sigma_alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  sigma_beta ~ normal(0, 5);
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 5);
  alpha_raw ~ normal(0, 1);
  beta_raw ~ normal(0, 1);

  alpha = mu_alpha + sigma_alpha * alpha_raw;
  beta = mu_beta + sigma_beta * beta_raw;
  for (n in 1:N) {
    for (t in 1:T) {
      mu_y[(n - 1) * T + t] = alpha[n] + beta[n] * time[t];
    }
  }
  y ~ normal(mu_y, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N": 5, "T": 5, "time": [0.0, 1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0], "y": [50, 58, 65, 72, 81, 48, 55, 61, 69, 76, 52, 61, 68, 75, 83, 47, 53, 59, 66, 72, 51, 59, 67, 73, 80]}"}
